url: "https://filipevascrocha.github.io/lexio/"
abstract: >-
  An R package for input-output models solved by preemptive
  (lexicographic) goal programming. The user declares an input-output
  database (technical structure, gross output, final demand, any number of
  satellite accounts as levels or coefficients and, optionally, a corridor
  on the economic deviations, on both sides, only below or only above) and
  the direction and goal of each account. Sectoral output is chosen to meet
  the goals in priority order, written as G x + d- - d+ = g. Each priority
  level is a linear program solved with GLPK, with the optima of the
  earlier levels locked. By default all k! priority orders of the k
  satellite accounts are run, with the economic block fixed at the last
  level; the operator may list the orderings to run, with several weighted
  goals per level, and move the economic block only by an explicit
  declaration. Every level of every run is reported, in tables and in an
  Excel workbook. The repository includes the replication of the doctoral
  thesis that introduced the model, on the Brazilian fuel and electricity
  markets with the 2018 input-output matrix with energy-sector detail
  published by EPE in partnership with FIPE, and the goal programming
  example of Miller and Blair.
keywords:
  - input-output
  - goal programming
  - lexicographic goal programming
  - satellite accounts
  - energy transition
  - Brazil
  - R
